==Jamaican Creole==

===Etymology===
{{rfe|lang=jam}}
Jamaican corruption of the English "All right."

IRIE is a pun on the Holy Name of God (Hari, Heli, Heru, El, et al). It is related to the Greek word Eirene meaning peace, itself a pun on the Holy Name. See Bhakti Ananda Goswami's research for further information on Holy Name punning!

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈairiː/|/ˈairɛː/|lang=jam}}

===Adjective===
{{infl|jam|adjective}}

# {{rasta|lang=jam}} feeling great;  [[cool]], [[good]], [[nice]]; A state of peacefulness or harmony, either within oneself or with the world in general.

